	"description" : "Chill One Piece cove\n\n[h2]Settings[/h2]\n[list]\n[*][b]Distant waves[/b]: ripples and swell on the open sea (0 = flat).\n[*][b]Sun glints[/b]: sparkles on the water (0 = off).\n[*][b]Extra caustics[/b]: a web of light in the shallows, faint at 50 and strong at 100 (0 = off).\n[*][b]Extra caustics speed[/b]: how fast that web moves (0 = still).\n[*][b]Wind on props[/b]: how much the hat, vest, bandana and map move (0 = still).\n[*][b]Plant sway[/b]: how much the plants move (0 = still).\n[*][b]Cigarette smoke[/b], [b]Cola fizz[/b], [b]Glass shine[/b], [b]Frost & cold vapour[/b]: the small prop effects (0 = off).\n[*][b]Cloud speed[/b]: how fast the clouds drift (0 = still).\n[*][b]Ultrawide framing[/b]: on wide screens, lower shows more sky, higher more of the ledge.\n[*][b]Render scale[/b]: lower it to save GPU on 4K screens or older cards.\n[/list]\nEvery slider at 50 is the tuned look. Brightness, contrast and colour are in Wallpaper Engine's own colour options. The frame rate follows its FPS setting.\n\n[h2]Video[/h2]\nhttps://youtu.be/HFNUrLrGlnk",
